  <!-- 5. INSIDE IRAN -->
  <div class="section" id="inside-iran">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Inside Iran
      <span class="meta">State-media decode &middot; ~200 words &middot; verb-ban + forecast-cite rule applies</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="inside-iran">
      <div class="iran-media-badges">
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRNA</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRIB</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Press TV</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Fars</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>
      <p>Iranian state media maintained a carefully bifurcated posture on the US-Iran deal track during June&nbsp;11-13. IRNA and Tasnim carried Foreign Ministry spokesperson Baghaei&rsquo;s June&nbsp;11 characterization of deal reports as &ldquo;speculation,&rdquo; while also transmitting Araghchi&rsquo;s more forward-leaning June&nbsp;13 framing &mdash; an internal calibration that kept Iran&rsquo;s official position within deniable range of the formal suspension while the FM&rsquo;s office advanced proximity to agreement. The IRGC&rsquo;s public skepticism of Trump&rsquo;s claims, transmitted via Tasnim, served its established institutional function of separating the military arm from any diplomatic retreat that the Foreign Ministry navigates. Mohsen Rezaei, military adviser to Supreme Leader, told Tasnim that Trump had agreed to partial release of Iran&rsquo;s frozen assets but declined to state so publicly &mdash; a framing constructed to present to domestic audiences that Iran extracted material concessions without yielding to US pressure narratives. The June&nbsp;1 suspension language has not been formally withdrawn in IRNA dispatches; this preserves the option to frame any resumed session as a new initiative rather than a reversal. Araghchi&rsquo;s reference to a two-stage structure with nuclear matters deferred to the second phase tracks the state media line that Iran did not capitulate on core red lines. → supports <span class="cite">F1</span>, supports <span class="cite">F2</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

